IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc1-support`

-- ccc1-s25-law-enforcement.l4 -- Part I (General), sections 25 and 25.1: protection of persons administering and enforcing the law, and the justification of public officers
-- and of persons acting at their direction for acts or omissions that would otherwise be offences (designation by a competent authority, senior officials, emergency designation).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30).
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- A justification ("is justified") is a defence. Where its "if" gate is not met the answer is JUST FALSE, read as "this section gives no justification on these facts" and never as "no defence at all"
-- (ruling of 2026-11-05 (b)). A "who" description that is not met answers NOTHING. A bar ("not justified unless", "no public officer is justified unless") is named as a bar: JUST TRUE = barred.
-- Answers of section 2 ("peace officer", "public officer", "bodily harm") are INPUTS, MAYBE BOOLEAN, carried through when NOTHING.
-- The official-only provisions (the designation powers of the competent authority and of a senior official) are encoded for what they mean to the person: whether a designation stands behind the justification of subsection (8).

§ `Section 25 -- Protection of persons acting under authority`

-- src:623 | Protection of persons acting under authority
-- src:624 | 25 (1) Every one who is required or authorized by law to do anything in the administration or enforcement of the law
-- src:625 | (a) as a private person,
-- src:626 | (b) as a peace officer or public officer,
-- src:627 | (c) in aid of a peace officer or public officer, or
-- src:628 | (d) by virtue of his office,
-- src:629 | is, if he acts on reasonable grounds, justified in doing what he is required or authorized to do and in using as much force as is necessary for that purpose.
@ref s 25(1) (src:623-629)
DECLARE `s 25(1) the capacity in which the person acts` IS ONE OF
    `s 25(1)(a) as a private person`
    `s 25(1)(b) as a peace officer or public officer`
    `s 25(1)(c) in aid of a peace officer or public officer`
    `s 25(1)(d) by virtue of his office`
    `s 25(1) in none of those capacities`

@ref s 25(1) (src:623-629)
GIVEN `the person is required or authorized by law to do the thing in the administration or enforcement of the law` IS A BOOLEAN
      capacity IS A `s 25(1) the capacity in which the person acts`
      `s 2 peace officer or public officer: the person is one` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person acts on reasonable grounds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25(1) the person is justified in doing what they are required or authorized to do` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person is required or authorized by law to do the thing in the administration or enforcement of the law` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every one who is required or authorized by law to do anything in the administration or enforcement of the law"
        IF capacity EQUALS `s 25(1) in none of those capacities` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): paragraphs (a) to (d) name four capacities and the list is not closed by "only"
        IF capacity EQUALS `s 25(1)(b) as a peace officer or public officer` AND `s 2 peace officer or public officer: the person is one` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is a peace officer or public officer is the answer of section 2, which was not given
        IF capacity EQUALS `s 25(1)(b) as a peace officer or public officer` AND `s 2 peace officer or public officer: the person is one` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "as a peace officer or public officer"
        IF NOT `the person acts on reasonable grounds` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is, if he acts on reasonable grounds, justified in doing what he is required or authorized to do"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 25(1) (src:623-629)
GIVEN `the person is justified in doing what they are required or authorized to do, by s 25(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the force used is as much as is necessary for that purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25(1) the person is justified in using as much force as is necessary for that purpose` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is justified in doing what they are required or authorized to do, by s 25(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND NOT `the force used is as much as is necessary for that purpose` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in using as much force as is necessary for that purpose"
        OTHERWISE `the person is justified in doing what they are required or authorized to do, by s 25(1)`

-- src:630 | Idem
-- src:631 | (2) Where a person is required or authorized by law to execute a process or to carry out a sentence, that person or any person who assists him is, if that person acts in good faith, justified in executing the process or in carrying out the sentence notwithstanding that the process or sentence is defective or that it was issued or imposed without jurisdiction or in excess of jurisdiction.
@ref s 25(2) (src:630-631)
GIVEN `the person is required or authorized by law to execute a process or to carry out a sentence, or is assisting a person who is` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person required or authorized acts in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the process or sentence is defective, or was issued or imposed without jurisdiction or in excess of jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25(2) the person is justified in executing the process or in carrying out the sentence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person is required or authorized by law to execute a process or to carry out a sentence, or is assisting a person who is` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a person is required or authorized by law to execute a process or to carry out a sentence, that person or any person who assists him is, if that person acts in good faith, justified in executing the process or in carrying out the sentence"
        IF NOT `the person required or authorized acts in good faith` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is, if that person acts in good faith, justified in executing the process or in carrying out the sentence"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE   -- whether or not `the process or sentence is defective, or was issued or imposed without jurisdiction or in excess of jurisdiction`: "notwithstanding that the process or sentence is defective"

-- src:632 | When not protected
-- src:633 | (3) Subject to subsections (4) and (5), a person is not justified for the purposes of subsection (1) in using force that is intended or is likely to cause death or grievous bodily harm unless the person believes on reasonable grounds that it is necessary for the self-preservation of the person or the preservation of any one under that person’s protection from death or grievous bodily harm.
@ref s 25(3) (src:632-633)
GIVEN `the force is intended or is likely to cause death or grievous bodily harm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person believes on reasonable grounds that it is necessary for the self-preservation of the person or the preservation of any one under that person's protection from death or grievous bodily harm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection (4) or (5) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25(3) subsection (3) bars justification under subsection (1) for the force` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the force is intended or is likely to cause death or grievous bodily harm` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in using force that is intended or is likely to cause death or grievous bodily harm"
        IF `subsection (4) or (5) applies` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to subsections (4) and (5)"
        IF `the person believes on reasonable grounds that it is necessary for the self-preservation of the person or the preservation of any one under that person's protection from death or grievous bodily harm` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the person believes on reasonable grounds that it is necessary for the self-preservation of the person or the preservation of any one under that person’s protection from death or grievous bodily harm"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:634 | When protected
-- src:635 | (4) A peace officer, and every person lawfully assisting the peace officer, is justified in using force that is intended or is likely to cause death or grievous bodily harm to a person to be arrested, if
-- src:636 | (a) the peace officer is proceeding lawfully to arrest, with or without warrant, the person to be arrested;
-- src:637 | (b) the offence for which the person is to be arrested is one for which that person may be arrested without warrant;
-- src:638 | (c) the person to be arrested takes flight to avoid arrest;
-- src:639 | (d) the peace officer or other person using the force believes on reasonable grounds that the force is necessary for the purpose of protecting the peace officer, the person lawfully assisting the peace officer or any other person from imminent or future death or grievous bodily harm; and
-- src:640 | (e) the flight cannot be prevented by reasonable means in a less violent manner.
@ref s 25(4) (src:634-640)
GIVEN `s 2 peace officer: the person is one` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is lawfully assisting the peace officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the peace officer is proceeding lawfully to arrest, with or without warrant, the person to be arrested` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence for which the person is to be arrested is one for which that person may be arrested without warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person to be arrested takes flight to avoid arrest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the peace officer or other person using the force believes on reasonable grounds that the force is necessary for the purpose of protecting the peace officer, the person lawfully assisting the peace officer or any other person from imminent or future death or grievous bodily harm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the flight cannot be prevented by reasonable means in a less violent manner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25(4) the person is justified in using force intended or likely to cause death or grievous bodily harm to the person to be arrested` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 2 peace officer: the person is one` EQUALS NOTHING AND NOT `the person is lawfully assisting the peace officer` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is a peace officer is the answer of section 2, which was not given
        IF `s 2 peace officer: the person is one` EQUALS JUST FALSE AND NOT `the person is lawfully assisting the peace officer` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A peace officer, and every person lawfully assisting the peace officer"
        IF `the peace officer is proceeding lawfully to arrest, with or without warrant, the person to be arrested`
           AND `the offence for which the person is to be arrested is one for which that person may be arrested without warrant`
           AND `the person to be arrested takes flight to avoid arrest`
           AND `the peace officer or other person using the force believes on reasonable grounds that the force is necessary for the purpose of protecting the peace officer, the person lawfully assisting the peace officer or any other person from imminent or future death or grievous bodily harm`
           AND `the flight cannot be prevented by reasonable means in a less violent manner`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is justified in using force that is intended or is likely to cause death or grievous bodily harm to a person to be arrested, if"

-- src:641 | Power in case of escape from penitentiary
-- src:642 | (5) A peace officer is justified in using force that is intended or is likely to cause death or grievous bodily harm against an inmate who is escaping from a penitentiary within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the Corrections and Conditional Release Act, if
-- src:643 | (a) the peace officer believes on reasonable grounds that any of the inmates of the penitentiary poses a threat of death or grievous bodily harm to the peace officer or any other person; and
-- src:644 | (b) the escape cannot be prevented by reasonable means in a less violent manner.
@ref s 25(5) (src:641-644)
GIVEN `s 2 peace officer: the person is one` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the inmate is escaping from a penitentiary within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the Corrections and Conditional Release Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the peace officer believes on reasonable grounds that any of the inmates of the penitentiary poses a threat of death or grievous bodily harm to the peace officer or any other person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the escape cannot be prevented by reasonable means in a less violent manner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25(5) the peace officer is justified in using force intended or likely to cause death or grievous bodily harm against the inmate` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 2 peace officer: the person is one` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is a peace officer is the answer of section 2, which was not given
        IF `s 2 peace officer: the person is one` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A peace officer is justified in using force"
        IF NOT `the inmate is escaping from a penitentiary within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the Corrections and Conditional Release Act` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "against an inmate who is escaping from a penitentiary within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the Corrections and Conditional Release Act"
        IF `the peace officer believes on reasonable grounds that any of the inmates of the penitentiary poses a threat of death or grievous bodily harm to the peace officer or any other person` AND `the escape cannot be prevented by reasonable means in a less violent manner` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is justified in using force that is intended or is likely to cause death or grievous bodily harm against an inmate who is escaping from a penitentiary within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the Corrections and Conditional Release Act, if"

§ `Section 25.1(1) -- Definitions for sections 25.1 to 25.4`

-- src:645 | Definitions
-- src:646 | 25.1 (1) The following definitions apply in this section and sections 25.2 to 25.4.
@ref s 25.1(1) (src:645-646)
DECLARE `s 25.1(1) the officer or official` IS ONE OF
    `s 25.1(1)(a) a member of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police`
    `s 25.1(1)(b) a member of a police service constituted under the laws of a province`
    `s 25.1(1)(c) any other public officer or senior official`
    `s 25.1(1) neither a public officer nor a senior official`

DECLARE `s 25.1(1) the competent authority` IS ONE OF
    `s 25.1(1)(a) the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness, personally`
    `s 25.1(1)(b) the Minister responsible for policing in the province, personally`
    `s 25.1(1)(c) the Minister who has responsibility for the Act of Parliament that the officer or official has the power to enforce, personally`

-- src:647 | competent authority means, with respect to a public officer or a senior official,
-- src:648 | (a) in the case of a member of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police, the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness, personally;
-- src:649 | (b) in the case of a member of a police service constituted under the laws of a province, the Minister responsible for policing in the province, personally; and
-- src:650 | (c) in the case of any other public officer or senior official, the Minister who has responsibility for the Act of Parliament that the officer or official has the power to enforce, personally. (autorité compétente)
@ref s 25.1(1) competent authority (src:647-650)
GIVEN person IS A `s 25.1(1) the officer or official`
GIVETH A MAYBE (`s 25.1(1) the competent authority`)
`s 25.1(1) the competent authority with respect to the public officer or senior official` MEANS
    CONSIDER person
    WHEN `s 25.1(1)(a) a member of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police` THEN JUST `s 25.1(1)(a) the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness, personally`
    WHEN `s 25.1(1)(b) a member of a police service constituted under the laws of a province` THEN JUST `s 25.1(1)(b) the Minister responsible for policing in the province, personally`
    WHEN `s 25.1(1)(c) any other public officer or senior official` THEN JUST `s 25.1(1)(c) the Minister who has responsibility for the Act of Parliament that the officer or official has the power to enforce, personally`
    WHEN `s 25.1(1) neither a public officer nor a senior official` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "means, with respect to a public officer or a senior official"

-- src:651 | public officer means a peace officer, or a public officer who has the powers of a peace officer under an Act of Parliament. (fonctionnaire public)
@ref s 25.1(1) public officer (src:651-651)
GIVEN `s 2 peace officer: the person is one` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 2 public officer: the person is one` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person has the powers of a peace officer under an Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25.1(1) the person is a public officer` MEANS
    `ccc1 either of` `s 2 peace officer: the person is one` (`ccc1 both of` `s 2 public officer: the person is one` (`ccc1 a fact as an answer` `the person has the powers of a peace officer under an Act of Parliament`))
    -- the answer is JUST FALSE only when both limbs say no ("public officer means a peace officer, or a public officer who has the powers of a peace officer under an Act of Parliament"), JUST TRUE when either holds, otherwise NOTHING

-- The answer that section 2 "justice system participant" (b)(viii.1) asks for (PLAN.md section 6, ccc1, seam [T]). PLAN.md types it BOOLEAN; it is MAYBE BOOLEAN here because the limb "a peace officer" of
-- section 25.1(1) depends on `s 2 peace officer`, which can answer NOTHING, and a caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
@ref s 25.1(1) public officer (src:651-651)
GIVEN `the person is a public officer, by s 25.1(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person acts at the direction of such an officer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25.1(1) the person is a public officer, or acts at the direction of one` MEANS
    `ccc1 either of` `the person is a public officer, by s 25.1(1)` (`ccc1 a fact as an answer` `the person acts at the direction of such an officer`)

-- src:652 | senior official means a senior official who is responsible for law enforcement and who is designated under subsection (5). (fonctionnaire supérieur)
@ref s 25.1(1) senior official (src:652-652)
GIVEN `the person is a senior official who is responsible for law enforcement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is designated under subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25.1(1) the person is a senior official` MEANS
    IF `the person is a senior official who is responsible for law enforcement` AND `the person is designated under subsection (5)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "senior official means a senior official who is responsible for law enforcement and who is designated under subsection (5)"

-- 25.1 (2): "Principle": a statement of the public interest that creates no rule (inert: not operative). It is quoted here and carried by no function.
-- src:653 | Principle
-- src:654 | (2) It is in the public interest to ensure that public officers may effectively carry out their law enforcement duties in accordance with the rule of law and, to that end, to expressly recognize in law a justification for public officers and other persons acting at their direction to commit acts or omissions that would otherwise constitute offences.

§ `Section 25.1(3) to (7) -- Designation`

-- src:655 | Designation of public officers
-- src:656 | (3) A competent authority may designate public officers for the purposes of this section and sections 25.2 to 25.4.
@ref s 25.1(3) (src:655-656)
GIVEN `the person making the designation is the competent authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person designated is a public officer, by s 25.1(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25.1(3) the competent authority may designate the person as a public officer for the purposes of sections 25.1 to 25.4` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person making the designation is the competent authority` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A competent authority may designate public officers"
        IF `the person designated is a public officer, by s 25.1(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may designate public officers"

-- src:657 | Condition — civilian oversight
-- src:658 | (3.1) A competent authority referred to in paragraph (a) or (b) of the definition of that term in subsection (1) may not designate any public officer under subsection (3) unless there is a public authority composed of persons who are not peace officers that may review the public officer’s conduct.
@ref s 25.1(3.1) (src:657-658)
GIVEN `the authority is one referred to in paragraph (a) or (b) of the definition of that term in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a public authority composed of persons who are not peace officers that may review the public officer's conduct` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25.1(3.1) the competent authority is barred from designating the public officer` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the authority is one referred to in paragraph (a) or (b) of the definition of that term in subsection (1)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A competent authority referred to in paragraph (a) or (b) of the definition of that term in subsection (1)"
        IF `there is a public authority composed of persons who are not peace officers that may review the public officer's conduct` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may not designate any public officer under subsection (3) unless there is a public authority composed of persons who are not peace officers that may review the public officer’s conduct"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:659 | Declaration as evidence
-- src:660 | (3.2) The Governor in Council or the lieutenant governor in council of a province, as the case may be, may designate a person or body as a public authority for the purposes of subsection (3.1), and that designation is conclusive evidence that the person or body is a public authority described in that subsection.
@ref s 25.1(3.2) (src:659-660)
GIVEN `the designation was made by the Governor in Council or the lieutenant governor in council of a province, as the case may be` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25.1(3.2) the designation is conclusive evidence that the person or body is a public authority described in subsection (3.1)` MEANS
    IF `the designation was made by the Governor in Council or the lieutenant governor in council of a province, as the case may be`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "that designation is conclusive evidence"

@ref s 25.1(3.2) (src:660-660)
GIVEN `the person making the designation is the Governor in Council or the lieutenant governor in council of a province, as the case may be` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25.1(3.2) the Governor in Council or the lieutenant governor in council may designate the person or body as a public authority` MEANS
    IF `the person making the designation is the Governor in Council or the lieutenant governor in council of a province, as the case may be`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Governor in Council or the lieutenant governor in council of a province, as the case may be, may designate a person or body as a public authority"

-- src:661 | Considerations
-- src:662 | (4) The competent authority shall make designations under subsection (3) on the advice of a senior official and shall consider the nature of the duties performed by the public officer in relation to law enforcement generally, rather than in relation to any particular investigation or enforcement activity.
@ref s 25.1(4) (src:661-662)
GIVEN `the designation is made on the advice of a senior official` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the competent authority considered the nature of the duties performed by the public officer in relation to law enforcement generally, rather than in relation to any particular investigation or enforcement activity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25.1(4) the designation was made as subsection (4) requires` MEANS
    IF `the designation is made on the advice of a senior official` AND `the competent authority considered the nature of the duties performed by the public officer in relation to law enforcement generally, rather than in relation to any particular investigation or enforcement activity`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection does not say that a designation made otherwise is not a designation

-- src:663 | Designation of senior officials
-- src:664 | (5) A competent authority may designate senior officials for the purposes of this section and sections 25.2 to 25.4.
@ref s 25.1(5) (src:663-664)
GIVEN `the person making the designation is the competent authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25.1(5) the competent authority may designate the person as a senior official for the purposes of sections 25.1 to 25.4` MEANS
    IF `the person making the designation is the competent authority`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A competent authority may designate senior officials"

-- src:665 | Emergency designation
-- src:666 | (6) A senior official may designate a public officer for the purposes of this section and sections 25.2 to 25.4 for a period of not more than 48 hours if the senior official is of the opinion that
-- src:667 | (a) by reason of exigent circumstances, it is not feasible for the competent authority to designate a public officer under subsection (3); and
-- src:668 | (b) in the circumstances of the case, the public officer would be justified in committing an act or omission that would otherwise constitute an offence.
@ref s 25.1(6) (src:665-668)
GIVEN `the person making the designation is a senior official, by s 25.1(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the period of the designation, in hours` IS A NUMBER
      `the senior official is of the opinion that, by reason of exigent circumstances, it is not feasible for the competent authority to designate a public officer under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the senior official is of the opinion that, in the circumstances of the case, the public officer would be justified in committing an act or omission that would otherwise constitute an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25.1(6) the senior official may designate the public officer` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person making the designation is a senior official, by s 25.1(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A senior official may designate a public officer"
        IF `the period of the designation, in hours` GREATER THAN 48 THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for a period of not more than 48 hours"
        IF `the senior official is of the opinion that, by reason of exigent circumstances, it is not feasible for the competent authority to designate a public officer under subsection (3)` AND `the senior official is of the opinion that, in the circumstances of the case, the public officer would be justified in committing an act or omission that would otherwise constitute an offence` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the senior official is of the opinion that"

-- src:669 | The senior official shall without delay notify the competent authority of the designation.
@ref s 25.1(6) notify (src:669-669)
