GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25.1(6) the senior official has notified the competent authority of the designation without delay` MEANS
    IF `the senior official has notified the competent authority of the designation` AND `the notice was given without delay`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The senior official shall without delay notify the competent authority of the designation."

-- src:670 | Conditions
-- src:671 | (7) A designation under subsection (3) or (6) may be made subject to conditions, including conditions limiting
-- src:672 | (a) the duration of the designation;
-- src:673 | (b) the nature of the conduct in the investigation of which a public officer may be justified in committing, or directing another person to commit, acts or omissions that would otherwise constitute an offence; and
-- src:674 | (c) the acts or omissions that would otherwise constitute an offence and that a public officer may be justified in committing or directing another person to commit.
@ref s 25.1(7) (src:670-674)
DECLARE `s 25.1(7) the condition limits` IS ONE OF
    `s 25.1(7)(a) the duration of the designation`
    `s 25.1(7)(b) the nature of the conduct in the investigation of which a public officer may be justified in committing, or directing another person to commit, acts or omissions that would otherwise constitute an offence`
    `s 25.1(7)(c) the acts or omissions that would otherwise constitute an offence and that a public officer may be justified in committing or directing another person to commit`
    `s 25.1(7) something else`

@ref s 25.1(7) (src:670-674)
GIVEN `the designation is made under subsection (3) or (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      limit IS A `s 25.1(7) the condition limits`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25.1(7) the designation may be made subject to the condition` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the designation is made under subsection (3) or (6)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A designation under subsection (3) or (6) may be made subject to conditions"
        IF limit EQUALS `s 25.1(7) something else` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "including conditions limiting"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 25.1(8) to (14) -- Justification, requirements, limits`

-- src:675 | Justification for acts or omissions
-- src:676 | (8) A public officer is justified in committing an act or omission — or in directing the commission of an act or omission under subsection (10) — that would otherwise constitute an offence if the public officer
-- src:677 | (a) is engaged in the investigation of an offence under, or the enforcement of, an Act of Parliament or in the investigation of criminal activity;
-- src:678 | (b) is designated under subsection (3) or (6); and
-- src:679 | (c) believes on reasonable grounds that the commission of the act or omission, as compared to the nature of the offence or criminal activity being investigated, is reasonable and proportional in the circumstances, having regard to such matters as the nature of the act or omission, the nature of the investigation and the reasonable availability of other means for carrying out the public officer’s law enforcement duties.
@ref s 25.1(8) (src:675-679)
GIVEN `the person is a public officer, by s 25.1(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the public officer is engaged in the investigation of an offence under, or the enforcement of, an Act of Parliament or in the investigation of criminal activity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the public officer is designated under subsection (3) or (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the public officer believes on reasonable grounds that the commission of the act or omission, as compared to the nature of the offence or criminal activity being investigated, is reasonable and proportional in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25.1(8) the public officer is justified in committing the act or omission` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is a public officer, by s 25.1(1)` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is a public officer is the answer of section 25.1(1) and of section 2, which was not given
        IF `the person is a public officer, by s 25.1(1)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A public officer is justified in committing an act or omission"
        IF `the public officer is engaged in the investigation of an offence under, or the enforcement of, an Act of Parliament or in the investigation of criminal activity`
           AND `the public officer is designated under subsection (3) or (6)`
           AND `the public officer believes on reasonable grounds that the commission of the act or omission, as compared to the nature of the offence or criminal activity being investigated, is reasonable and proportional in the circumstances`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that would otherwise constitute an offence if the public officer"

-- src:680 | Requirements for certain acts
-- src:681 | (9) No public officer is justified in committing an act or omission that would otherwise constitute an offence and that would be likely to result in loss of or serious damage to property, or in directing the commission of an act or omission under subsection (10), unless, in addition to meeting the conditions set out in paragraphs (8)(a) to (c), he or she
-- src:682 | (a) is personally authorized in writing to commit the act or omission — or direct its commission — by a senior official who believes on reasonable grounds that committing the act or omission, as compared to the nature of the offence or criminal activity being investigated, is reasonable and proportional in the circumstances, having regard to such matters as the nature of the act or omission, the nature of the investigation and the reasonable availability of other means for carrying out the public officer’s law enforcement duties; or
-- src:683 | (b) believes on reasonable grounds that the grounds for obtaining an authorization under paragraph (a) exist but it is not feasible in the circumstances to obtain the authorization and that the act or omission is necessary to
-- src:684 | (i) preserve the life or safety of any person,
-- src:685 | (ii) prevent the compromise of the identity of a public officer acting in an undercover capacity, of a confidential informant or of a person acting covertly under the direction and control of a public officer, or
-- src:686 | (iii) prevent the imminent loss or destruction of evidence of an indictable offence.
@ref s 25.1(9) (src:680-686)
DECLARE `s 25.1(9)(b) what the act or omission is necessary to do` IS ONE OF
    `s 25.1(9)(b)(i) preserve the life or safety of any person`
    `s 25.1(9)(b)(ii) prevent the compromise of the identity of a public officer acting in an undercover capacity, of a confidential informant or of a person acting covertly under the direction and control of a public officer`
    `s 25.1(9)(b)(iii) prevent the imminent loss or destruction of evidence of an indictable offence`
    `s 25.1(9)(b) none of those things`

@ref s 25.1(9) (src:680-686)
GIVEN `the act or omission would be likely to result in loss of or serious damage to property, or is a directing of an act or omission under subsection (10)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conditions set out in paragraphs (8)(a) to (c) are met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the public officer is personally authorized in writing to commit the act or omission, or direct its commission, by a senior official who believes on reasonable grounds that committing it, as compared to the nature of the offence or criminal activity being investigated, is reasonable and proportional in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the public officer believes on reasonable grounds that the grounds for obtaining an authorization under paragraph (a) exist but it is not feasible in the circumstances to obtain the authorization` IS A BOOLEAN
      necessary IS A `s 25.1(9)(b) what the act or omission is necessary to do`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25.1(9) subsection (9) bars the public officer's justification` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the act or omission would be likely to result in loss of or serious damage to property, or is a directing of an act or omission under subsection (10)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an act or omission that would otherwise constitute an offence and that would be likely to result in loss of or serious damage to property, or in directing the commission of an act or omission under subsection (10)"
        IF `the conditions set out in paragraphs (8)(a) to (c) are met` AND `the public officer is personally authorized in writing to commit the act or omission, or direct its commission, by a senior official who believes on reasonable grounds that committing it, as compared to the nature of the offence or criminal activity being investigated, is reasonable and proportional in the circumstances` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless, in addition to meeting the conditions set out in paragraphs (8)(a) to (c), he or she (a) is personally authorized in writing"
        IF `the conditions set out in paragraphs (8)(a) to (c) are met` AND `the public officer believes on reasonable grounds that the grounds for obtaining an authorization under paragraph (a) exist but it is not feasible in the circumstances to obtain the authorization` AND NOT (necessary EQUALS `s 25.1(9)(b) none of those things`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "or (b) believes on reasonable grounds that the grounds for obtaining an authorization under paragraph (a) exist but it is not feasible in the circumstances to obtain the authorization and that the act or omission is necessary to"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:687 | Person acting at direction of public officer
-- src:688 | (10) A person who commits an act or omission that would otherwise constitute an offence is justified in committing it if
-- src:689 | (a) a public officer directs him or her to commit that act or omission and the person believes on reasonable grounds that the public officer has the authority to give that direction; and
-- src:690 | (b) he or she believes on reasonable grounds that the commission of that act or omission is for the purpose of assisting the public officer in the public officer’s law enforcement duties.
@ref s 25.1(10) (src:687-690)
GIVEN `a public officer directs the person to commit the act or omission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person believes on reasonable grounds that the public officer has the authority to give that direction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person believes on reasonable grounds that the commission of the act or omission is for the purpose of assisting the public officer in the public officer's law enforcement duties` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25.1(10) the person is justified in committing the act or omission at the direction of a public officer` MEANS
    IF `a public officer directs the person to commit the act or omission`
       AND `the person believes on reasonable grounds that the public officer has the authority to give that direction`
       AND `the person believes on reasonable grounds that the commission of the act or omission is for the purpose of assisting the public officer in the public officer's law enforcement duties`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is justified in committing it if"

-- src:691 | Limitation
-- src:692 | (11) Nothing in this section justifies
-- src:693 | (a) the intentional or criminally negligent causing of death or bodily harm to another person;
-- src:694 | (b) the wilful attempt in any manner to obstruct, pervert or defeat the course of justice; or
-- src:695 | (c) conduct that would violate the sexual integrity of an individual.
@ref s 25.1(11) (src:691-695)
DECLARE `s 25.1(11) the conduct` IS ONE OF
    `s 25.1(11)(a) the intentional or criminally negligent causing of death or bodily harm to another person`
    `s 25.1(11)(b) the wilful attempt in any manner to obstruct, pervert or defeat the course of justice`
    `s 25.1(11)(c) conduct that would violate the sexual integrity of an individual`
    `s 25.1(11) other conduct`

@ref s 25.1(11) (src:691-695)
GIVEN conduct IS A `s 25.1(11) the conduct`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25.1(11) the section justifies the conduct` MEANS
    CONSIDER conduct
    WHEN `s 25.1(11)(a) the intentional or criminally negligent causing of death or bodily harm to another person` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section justifies (a) the intentional or criminally negligent causing of death or bodily harm to another person"
    WHEN `s 25.1(11)(b) the wilful attempt in any manner to obstruct, pervert or defeat the course of justice` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) the wilful attempt in any manner to obstruct, pervert or defeat the course of justice"
    WHEN `s 25.1(11)(c) conduct that would violate the sexual integrity of an individual` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) conduct that would violate the sexual integrity of an individual"
    WHEN `s 25.1(11) other conduct` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (11) names three kinds of conduct and says nothing of other conduct

-- src:696 | Protection, defences and immunities unaffected
-- src:697 | (12) Nothing in this section affects the protection, defences and immunities of peace officers and other persons recognized under the law of Canada.
@ref s 25.1(12) (src:696-697)
GIVEN `the protection, defence or immunity of a peace officer or other person is recognized under the law of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25.1(12) the section affects the protection, defences and immunities recognized under the law of Canada` MEANS
    IF `the protection, defence or immunity of a peace officer or other person is recognized under the law of Canada`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section affects the protection, defences and immunities of peace officers and other persons recognized under the law of Canada."
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "recognized under the law of Canada"

-- src:698 | Compliance with requirements
-- src:699 | (13) Nothing in this section relieves a public officer of criminal liability for failing to comply with any other requirements that govern the collection of evidence.
@ref s 25.1(13) (src:698-699)
GIVEN `the requirement is another requirement that governs the collection of evidence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25.1(13) the section relieves the public officer of criminal liability for failing to comply with the requirement` MEANS
    IF `the requirement is another requirement that governs the collection of evidence`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section relieves a public officer of criminal liability for failing to comply with any other requirements that govern the collection of evidence."
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any other requirements that govern the collection of evidence"

-- src:700 | Exception — Controlled Drugs and Substances Act and Cannabis Act
-- src:701 | (14) Nothing in this section justifies a public officer or a person acting at his or her direction in committing an act or omission — or a public officer in directing the commission of an act or omission — that constitutes an offence under a provision of Part I of the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act or of the regulations made under it or a provision of Division 1 of Part 1 of the Cannabis Act.
@ref s 25.1(14) (src:700-701)
GIVEN `the act or omission constitutes an offence under a provision of Part I of the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act or of the regulations made under it or a provision of Division 1 of Part 1 of the Cannabis Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25.1(14) the section justifies the act or omission` MEANS
    IF `the act or omission constitutes an offence under a provision of Part I of the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act or of the regulations made under it or a provision of Division 1 of Part 1 of the Cannabis Act`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section justifies a public officer or a person acting at his or her direction in committing an act or omission"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offence under a provision of Part I of the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act"

-- The justification of a public officer, with the three limits that follow it: (9), (11) and (14). A limit that bars the justification makes the answer JUST FALSE; otherwise the answer is that of subsection (8).
@ref s 25.1(8), (9), (11), (14) (a composition of four subsections: no quotation)
GIVEN `the answer of subsection (8)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of subsection (9): barred` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of subsection (11): the section justifies the conduct` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of subsection (14): the section justifies the act or omission` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25.1 the public officer is justified, subject to subsections (9), (11) and (14)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the answer of subsection (9): barred` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No public officer is justified in committing an act or omission that would otherwise constitute an offence"
        IF `the answer of subsection (11): the section justifies the conduct` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section justifies"
        IF `the answer of subsection (14): the section justifies the act or omission` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section justifies a public officer or a person acting at his or her direction in committing an act or omission"
        OTHERWISE `the answer of subsection (8)`
